7day":"Medium","idp_source":"gtwo_kml_202611191142","idp_filedate":1795088550000,"nhcTitle":"Offshore of the Southeast U.S. Coast","discussion":"Disorganized showers and thunderstorms near the northwestern Bahamas  and Florida are associated with a frontal system.  A non-tropical  low pressure system is expected to form along the front near the  northwest Bahamas on Friday.  This system could become a subtropical  or tropical storm while it moves northward or northeastward near or  just offshore of the southeastern U.S. coast through the weekend.   Regardless of development, strong winds, dangerous surf, and coastal  flooding are likely along portions of the southeast and mid-Atlantic  coasts into early next week.  Interests along the eastern U.S. coast  should monitor the progress of this system. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...20 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...60 percent.","disturbance":1}}]}